# expected-project — settings

**The user's standing directives for this project.** This is the one file in the agentic layer whose
author is the **user**: an agent may propose a change and must not decide one.

> These are **choices**, not rules. The rules are in `.critos/system/` and do not vary between
> projects. If something here contradicts a system contract, the contract wins — except where the
> contract explicitly says a project may specialize it.

---

## Language

**Everything written and persisted is English** — repo content (code, comments, docs, UI strings,
migration and SQL headers), git history (commit messages, branch names, tags), and strings the
system emits (logs, errors, UI copy). Two carve-outs, and only these:

- **Live chat with the user**: any language.
- **Data is not an artifact**: observed/captured values (names, labels, scraped text) stay as
  captured — a foreign-language value is a fact, not prose.

> ⚠️ **This setting does not reach inside `.critos/`.** Everything in the agentic layer is **English,
> always**, whatever this says — it is not an editorial preference but the format of the substrate the
> method itself reads, parses and migrates (`contract-system § Substrate invariants`). The same holds
> for UTC and absolute dates.

